      "extract_value": "This section reports preliminary analyses comparing women and men, noting that subscale means, standard deviations, and correlations for women and men are presented in Table 2. A 2 \u00d7 6 MANOVA revealed significant differences between women and men, and univariate tests indicated men had significantly higher BMI and lower levels of perceived pressure to be lean from family, body dissatisfaction, and disordered eating.",
      "evidence_source": "Subscale means, standard deviations, and correlations for women and men are located in Table 2. A 2 \u00d7 6 multivariate analysis of variance (MANOVA) revealed differences between women and men, F(6, 281) = 14.90, p < .001, Wilks's \u039b = .76. Univariate tests indicated that men had significantly higher BMI, F(1, 286) = 8.46, p < .01 and lower levels of perceived pressure to be lean from family, F(1, 286) = 9.68, p < .01; body dissatisfaction, F(1, 286) = 30.23, p < .001; and disordered eating, F(1, 286) = 13.21, p < .001.",
